Import File
Imports a list which you saved beforehand. The command opens the dialog box Open.
Remarks
Double-click the name of a list/table which you exported before with the commands Export Text File or
Export Object File or click the name once and then click Open.
You can open files of these types:
Plant Simulation automatically recognizes the encoding of a text file when opening it.
• To open a Plant Simulation object file, select the file type Object Files (*.pslist) from the drop-down list
and the name of the file and click Open.
The Plant Simulation object file contains the contents and the Plant Simulation-format of the list, for
example settings about the data format, the dimension of the list, index and column widths, etc. This
way you can exchange lists between different Plant Simulation simulation models. Plant Simulation
opens it with all values and formats, which you saved with the extension .psobj. Other programs do not
recognize this proprietary format.
• To open a text file, select the file type Text Files (*.txt) from the drop-down list and the name of the file
and click Open.
A text file only contains the contents of the list. It does not save any settings that are specific to Plant
Simulation. You can also create a text file in a text editor or spreadsheet application and then open it as
a *.txt file in a Plant Simulation list. The format of the text file is described under Text File Format.
• To open an Excel workbook, select the file type Excel Workbooks (*.xls, .xlsx, xlsm, xlsb) from the
drop-down list and the name of the file and click Open.
Note
Plant Simulation uses Excel as COM-server when reading and writing MS Excel-files. For this reason
MS Excel has to be installed on your computer. To continue using the previous, no longer supported
Excel interface, you can use the start option -NativeExcel.
Import File
11-3828 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Note
We import the raw values from Excel and convert the data in Plant Simulation itself. When importing
date into columns of data type string we convert numerical values in Plant Simulation. The Plant
Simulation format might not match the format that was set in Excel.
If Plant Simulation reads an MS Excel table, it attempts to convert the values in the individual column to
the data types of the columns in your Plant Simulation table. This only works if you created the columns
on the Excel worksheets so that they only contain a single data type, meaning that, if you, for example,
assign the data type String to a cell of the specified column, the entire column may only be of data type
String.
Row 0 (zero) is the exception: If the Excel table, which Plant Simulation reads, has a column index, it
interprets row 0 as the column index, and it will not be part of the data type designation of the columns.
When importing data Plant Simulation considers the dimension of the DataTable. Suppose you set the
number of rows to 3 and the number of columns to 10, then Plant Simulation only imports the first 3
rows and the first 10 columns. This way you can improve the performance of large tables if you do not
need all data from the Excel file.
See also
readFile [SimTalk] - lists
readExcelFile [SimTalk]
readXMLFile [SimTalk]
Specifying Start Options, -NativeExcel
Import File
Plant Simulation Help 11-3829
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

