Text File Format
Opens the dialog Text File Format enabling you to select settings for exporting text files.
Remarks
When you save or open a list as a text file (*.txt), the settings you select determine how Plant Simulation
saves data and how it interprets it when opening the text file. Plant Simulation exports and imports data
row by row.
• Select a Column Separator:
Tab, Space, Semicolon, or Comma.
Note
We strongly advise against using the comma (,) as Column Separator as well as as the Decimal
Separator. Use it only as either the Column Separator or as the Decimal Separator.
• Select a Decimal Separator for exporting or importing a list:
(Period) or (Comma).
• Select how Plant Simulation saves and opens entries of data type time from the drop-down list Time
format.
You can pick S for seconds, M:S for minutes:seconds, H:M:S for hours:minutes:seconds or D:H:M:S for
days:hours:minutes:seconds.
This way you can save values of data type time in a format that spreadsheet applications that cannot
read our internal time format, also recognize.
