Edit Format
Opens the dialog Edit Format. Edit Settings, Permissions, the Dimension, and the Data Type of the list
here.
Remarks
The dialog Edit Format shows different tabs depending on what you select:
• Select one or several cells, or a range of cells spanning several columns, to show the Tab Settings and
the Tab Permissions. The settings you select here apply to the selected cell or range of cells.
Edit Format
11-3856 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Select one or several columns, by clicking the column header, to show the Tab Data Type and the Tab
Dimension in addition. The settings you select here apply to the selected column or range of columns.
• Select the entire list, by clicking the Select All button 
 , to make the settings you select apply
to the entire list.
Edit Format
Plant Simulation Help 11-3857
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

The box Range shows the selected range of cells or columns. In our example above this encompasses the
cell in column 1, row 1 to the greatest valid column and row index.
Click Apply to apply the settings you modified for the selected range. After you clicked Apply, you can
select another range and select settings for that range, etc. without having to close the dialog.
Click OK to apply the settings and close the dialog.
Click Cancel to discard your changes.
