Column Index Belongs to Contents
To set that the column index belongs to the contents of the DataTable, select this check box.
Remarks
Selecting the check box causes the column index to be inherited together with the contents of the
DataTable if Inherit Contents 
  is active.
To set that the column index belongs to the format of the DataTable, clear the check box. Then the
column index is inherited together with the format of the DataTable if Inherit Format 
  is active.
When you create a new model the setting is deactivated by default. For new models the column index
belongs to the format and will thus be inherited when you deactivate inheritance of the contents.
Note
Entering the range of cells has different effects on SimTalk instructions, depending whether Column
Index Belongs to Contents is activated or not.
Note
Only the DataTable provides this setting.
SimTalk
DataTable.delete [SimTalk] - lists
