Common Format [check box]
Plant Simulation shows the check box Common Format instead of the text box Format String and adds
the Tab Contents. This applies to or the data types Table, List, Stack and Queue.
Remarks
To force all lists in the range displayed into the same format, select Common Format. Then click the Tab
Contents and create a template list there. Lists you create after this will take all formatting properties you
selected here, compare Creating Lists within Lists and Tables.
If you activated Common Format for a column, assigning a subtable to a table cell creates a copy of the
assigned table. Otherwise, Plant Simulation enters a reference to the assigned table. The reason for this
is that it does not make sense to specify a reference if Common Format is active as the assigned table
should not be subject to the common format.
SimTalk
