Activating and Deactivating Common Format
Describes how to activate and deactivate the setting Common Format
Remarks
Suppose you created a list within a table and assigned this list to the local variable named l (lower case l).
• In the first example we selected the check box Common Format. The following Method uses a local
variable to access a list in a table. Here Plant Simulation accesses a reference to the list.
If you activated Common Format for a column, assigning a subtable to a table cell creates a copy of the
assigned table. Otherwise Plant Simulation enters a reference to the assigned table. The reason for this
is that it does not make sense to specify a reference when Common Format is active as the assigned
table should not be subject to the common format.
var l: list[string]
MyDataTable.delete
MyDataTable.createNestedList
l := MyDataTable[2,1]            // reference
l.insert(1,"abc")
l.insert(1,"Hello")
print MyDataTable[2,1].read(1)  //abc
print MyDataTable[2,1].read(2 ) // Hello
• In the second example, we cleared the check box Common Format. Here you arrive at the same result
by assigning a local list with the same format. Now the format is determined by the local variable, not by
the table.
var l:list[string]
MyDataTable.delete
l.createNestedList
Activating and Deactivating Common Format
Plant Simulation Help 11-3877
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

l.insert(1,"abc")
MyDataTable[2,1] := l
l.insert(1,"Hello")
print MyDataTable[2,1].read(1) // abc
print MyDataTable[2,1].read(2) // Hello 
Note
If you assign a list or table to a cell with list or table format, and you selected Common Format, Plant
Simulation may create a copy of the list instead of creating a reference, depending on the format of
the list or table you assigned.
SimTalk
setCommonFormat [SimTalk]
setCommonFormatData [SimTalk] - DataTable
getCommonFormatData [SimTalk] - DataTable
CommonFormatColumnIndex [SimTalk]
Activating and Deactivating Common Format
11-3878 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Data Type for the Column Index
Describes how to set the data type of the column index of a table.
Remarks
Proceed as follows to set the data type of the column index:
• Click Activate Column Index on the List ribbon tab to activate it.
• Select the column of the column index, i.e., the column with the number 0.
• Click Format on the List ribbon tab. Select the data type from the drop-down list. For the data types
integer, real, and string you can also type in a Format String.
• Select the check box Fast Index Access to gain fast access to the user-defined column indexes.
• Select the check box Unique Index Key to only allow unique entries in user-defined indexes, depending
on the data type.
Note
Plant Simulation highlights the cell in red and shows a message if you try to type in an expression that
already exists. Plant Simulation does not show a message if you assign an expression, that already
exists, to an index in a Method!
SimTalk
DataTypeColumnIndex [SimTalk]
Data Type for the Column Index
Plant Simulation Help 11-3879
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Fast Index Access [columns]
To allow for quickly accessing the user-defined column/row index, select this check box. Then, Plant
Simulation internally creates a data structure that reduces the search effort, but slightly increases memory
usage and the time required for changing the index.
Remarks
If you select the row of the column index, which is located above the first row of cells of the list/table, and
then click Format on the List ribbon tab, the dialog List Format > Data Type shows the check box Fast
Index Access.
The more columns and rows your table has, the more you benefit from the improved access speed.
Note
If the table contains a large number of entries, we recommend to activate Fast Index Access.
SimTalk
FastAccessColumnIndex [SimTalk]
Fast Index Access [columns]
11-3880 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Unique Index Key [columns]
To only allow unique entries in user-defined indexes, depending on the data type, select this check box.
Plant Simulation shows a warning if you try to assign an entry that already exists.
Remarks
If you select the column of the column index, which is located above the first row of cells of the list/table,
and then select Format > Format > List Format > Data Type, Plant Simulation shows the check box
Unique Index Key.
If you assign an entry for an index that already exists in a Method, Plant Simulation does not show a
warning message!
SimTalk
