Describes how to set the data type of the row index of a table.
Remarks
Proceed as follows to set the data type of the row index:
• Click Activate Row Index on the List ribbon tab to activate it.
• Select the column of the row index, i.e., the row with the number 0.
• Click Format on the List ribbon tab. Select the data type from the drop-down list. For the data types
integer, real, and string you can also type in a Format String.
• Select the check box Fast Index Access to gain fast access to the user-defined column indexes.
• Select the check box Unique Index Key to only allow unique entries in user-defined indexes, depending
on the data type.
Plant Simulation highlights the cell in red and shows a message if you try to enter an expression that
already exists.
