Inheritance [general description]
Inherit Format [button]
11-3888 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Inherit Contents [lists]
Turns inheritance of the contents of the list off or on.
Remarks
When you insert a list into a Frame, it automatically inherits its contents from its class. You can only
change the contents of the new, instantiated list after you turn Inherit Contents off. Turning off this
command also turns off Inherit Format [button]. Typing data into a list or table automatically turns
Inherit Contents off.
Note
Plant Simulation does not turn Inherit Contents off, when you instantiate the class of a list containing a
sublist, and then write to the instance with a Method, or when you write to the sublist with a Method. If
you model like that, you have to turn Inherit Contents off yourself.
