Import [embedded objects]
To import a tab-delimited text file containing information which you would like to import into the list,
select this command.
Remarks
You can Import a list, which you Exported from another list, or which you were provided with as a file
from colleagues or customers, in one of the following formats:
• Object files with the extension .pslist.
• Text files with the extension .txt.
• Excel Workbooks with the extensions .xls, .xlsc, .xlsm, or .xlsb.
• XML files with the extension .xml.
Note
Importing a file only works correctly if the file contains the Name of the attribute.
It does not work correctly if the file only contains the Alias of the attribute.
Import [embedded objects]
11-3910 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Import [embedded objects]
Plant Simulation Help 11-3911
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Export [embedded objects]
To export the contents of the list to a tab-delimited text file, select this command.
Remarks
You can select one of these formats:
• ANSI Text Files saves the list with ANSI encoding.
ANSI is an 8-bit character set that enables you to represent up to 256 characters (0 through 255). The
ANSI character set is a superset of the 7-bit ASCII character set.
• UTF-8 Text Files saves the list with UTF-8 encoding.
UTF-8 is another encoding of the Unicode character set. Each character is represented by one to three
bytes.
• Unicode Text Files saves the list with Unicode encoding.
Unicode is a 16-bit character set that includes almost all of the written languages of the world. Plant
Simulation saves Unicode in UTF-16 encoding. Each character is represented by two bytes.
• Excel Workbooks saves the list as an Excel file with the extension .xls.
If you scroll to the top on the left-hand side in the dialog Save As, Plant Simulation shows the folder to
which the list files with the respective formats are saved.
You can then Import this file into another list.
Export [embedded objects]
11-3912 Plant Simulation Help
