Accessing a Range of Cells with a Method
Accessing a Range of Cells with a Method
You can not only access individual entries in a single cell of the lists, but you can also process a contiguous
range of cells.
Remarks
A number of methods, such as min, max, only apply to a range. If you access a range of cells, you have to
use a special syntax.
We differentiate between
• Cell Ranges in Lists with One Column
• Cell Ranges in Tables with Several Columns
Ranges in Lists with One Column
Cell Ranges in Lists with One Column
Access a cell range in a list with one column by typing in the left curly brace {, the number of the first cell
in the range, the right curly brace }, two periods .., the left curly brace {, the number of the last cell in
the range, and the closing curly brace }.
Sort Descending [context menu, lists]
